16	// status_truth_test.go pins the one promise `status` exists to keep: the word
17	// "healthy" means the brain can be read. Two states broke it, and they are the
18	// two states in which nothing was ever built, so every counter the verdict
19	// summed read zero:
20	//
21	//   - no brain at all (a repo that was never onboarded, or one just reset), and
22	//   - a brain whose manifest declares no semantic index.
23	//
24	// A third state -- a semantic SQLite store shredded under a manifest that still
25	// describes it -- was reported as unhealthy but not usefully: the verdict was
26	// the single word "unsafe" plus a pointer to `doctor`, which rebuilds nothing
27	// and printed strictly less than `status --verbose` already did.
